WEBVTT

00:02.151 --> 00:03.191
This time will be different.

00:03.271 --> 00:04.771
Subaru?
What's wrong?

00:04.861 --> 00:05.781
Can you move?

00:05.861 --> 00:06.981
Can you talk?

00:08.651 --> 00:10.071
[sighs]

00:10.151 --> 00:12.201
[gasps]

00:14.621 --> 00:15.741
Emilia.

00:15.831 --> 00:17.251
[BEATRICE]
Emilia isn't the only one

00:17.331 --> 00:18.581
who was worried about you.

00:18.661 --> 00:20.081
Oh!

00:20.161 --> 00:21.581
Ah!

00:21.671 --> 00:23.461
What's that look for,
I suppose?

00:23.541 --> 00:25.881
It's almost as if you can't
believe the adorable Betty

00:25.961 --> 00:27.511
is standing right before you.

00:27.591 --> 00:28.671
Beatrice!

00:28.761 --> 00:29.681
Beatrice!

00:29.761 --> 00:31.431
Oh, Beatrice!

00:31.511 --> 00:32.551
What the heck?

00:32.641 --> 00:34.431
This is too sudden, I suppose.

00:34.511 --> 00:36.971
It's just you--
you really--

00:37.061 --> 00:39.561
you have a face that makes
me feel at ease and happy.

00:39.641 --> 00:41.561
It's so cute that I
feel like I'm back home.

00:41.651 --> 00:43.191
I could fall in love.

00:43.271 --> 00:45.021
You know, I really don't
want to believe you meant that

00:45.111 --> 00:46.781
as a compliment, so I won't.

00:46.861 --> 00:49.821
Please, Subaru, don't mess
with us right when you wake up.

00:49.901 --> 00:51.571
We still don't even
know why you passed out.

00:51.651 --> 00:53.701
So when you act
like that, you--

00:55.491 --> 00:56.701
Subaru?

00:56.791 --> 00:58.621
[crying]

00:58.701 --> 01:01.621
[emotional music]

01:01.711 --> 01:03.541
♪ ♪

01:03.621 --> 01:05.291
What's wrong, I suppose?

01:05.381 --> 01:06.501
It's all right.

01:06.591 --> 01:08.501
Betty will be right
here by your side.

01:08.591 --> 01:10.511
[SUBARU cries]

01:10.591 --> 01:12.471
♪ ♪

01:12.551 --> 01:14.761
No need for tears, Subaru.

01:14.851 --> 01:17.471
Just take slow, deep breaths.

01:17.561 --> 01:19.221
Calm down.

01:19.311 --> 01:21.021
Beatrice is here.

01:21.101 --> 01:22.271
And so am I.

01:22.351 --> 01:23.811
We've got you.

01:23.901 --> 01:25.731
[crying]

01:25.811 --> 01:32.901
♪ ♪

01:34.031 --> 01:36.871
[theme music]

01:36.951 --> 01:40.411
♪ ♪

01:40.491 --> 01:42.751
[singing]

01:42.831 --> 01:49.881
♪ ♪

03:04.331 --> 03:05.911
[SUBARU]
So that's how it is.

03:06.001 --> 03:07.211
It seems like I
lost my memories

03:07.291 --> 03:08.751
when I was in the archive.

03:08.831 --> 03:11.251
This might cause a lot
of trouble for you guys,

03:11.341 --> 03:14.261
but I appreciate all
of you bearing with me.

03:14.341 --> 03:18.051
I know you're all really
worried about Subaru right now,

03:18.141 --> 03:21.141
but it's important for all
of us to keep it together.

03:21.221 --> 03:23.891
I'm sure no one feels
more anxious than he does.

03:23.971 --> 03:26.021
It doesn't look
that way to me.

03:26.101 --> 03:29.271
Tell me, what kind of dumb
act is this, Barusu?

03:29.351 --> 03:30.691
This isn't an act
or something.

03:30.771 --> 03:32.231
I'm being super
serious about telling

03:32.311 --> 03:33.941
you all the whole truth.

03:34.021 --> 03:36.701
And honestly, my heart's about
to explode from the anxiety.

03:36.781 --> 03:38.201
So your acting has improved.

03:38.281 --> 03:39.951
You think if you speak
confidently, we'll simply--

03:40.031 --> 03:41.951
[BEATRICE] Subaru isn't the
kind of person that would hurt

03:42.031 --> 03:44.121
us by telling such cruel lies.

03:44.201 --> 03:46.711
You should know that as well
as anyone, I suppose.

03:46.791 --> 03:47.911
Mm.

03:50.211 --> 03:52.631
Oh, well, what
are we gonna do?

03:52.711 --> 03:55.091
You're just completely
hopeless, aren't you?

03:55.171 --> 03:56.881
[gasps]

03:56.961 --> 03:59.091
Why the heck did
you react like that?

03:59.181 --> 04:02.051
Seriously, you look like you
just saw a ghost or something.

04:02.141 --> 04:03.301
Talk about rude.

04:03.391 --> 04:04.681
[creepy noise]

04:04.761 --> 04:05.721
Hey, Meili.

04:05.811 --> 04:07.311
[MEILI]
Interesting.

04:07.391 --> 04:09.561
So at the very least you
still remember my name, huh?

04:09.641 --> 04:10.771
OK, then.

04:10.851 --> 04:13.111
In that case,
what did you forget?

04:13.191 --> 04:14.521
[SUBARU]
A lot, unfortunately,

04:14.611 --> 04:16.481
I lost what they call
episodic memory.

04:16.571 --> 04:19.111
I can still remember the names
of most people and things,

04:19.201 --> 04:21.361
but when it comes
to experiences with them,

04:21.451 --> 04:23.661
it gets pretty murky.

04:23.741 --> 04:25.911
All right,
so does that include,

04:25.991 --> 04:27.411
say, what happened yesterday?

04:27.501 --> 04:29.331
Mm.

04:29.411 --> 04:30.461
It does.

04:30.541 --> 04:33.041
[JULIUS]
All of yesterday, huh?

04:33.131 --> 04:34.541
I see.

04:34.631 --> 04:36.381
Yes, I suppose so.

04:36.461 --> 04:39.341
[SHAULA] Again, Master,
are you for really real?

04:39.421 --> 04:41.051
Are you gonna keep
forgetting me over and over

04:41.131 --> 04:43.051
until I die alone?

04:43.141 --> 04:46.391
[ECHIDNA] Frankly, it's a bit
difficult to accept that truth,

04:46.471 --> 04:49.481
but still, it's likely there's
a trap in this tower that

04:49.561 --> 04:51.391
left Natsuki in this state.

04:51.481 --> 04:53.271
I think it's important
that we tread carefully.

04:53.351 --> 04:54.901
Mm.

04:54.981 --> 04:57.401
The most likely place is
the archive where Emilia

04:57.481 --> 04:59.281
and Beatrice discovered me.

04:59.361 --> 05:02.031
I mean, it's been shady
from the beginning.

05:02.111 --> 05:03.031
Um--

05:04.411 --> 05:07.201
Anyway, I'm sorry I
scared you all like that.

05:07.281 --> 05:09.621
I'm sure we all need a bit
of time to process everything,

05:09.701 --> 05:11.291
so let's take a break.

05:11.371 --> 05:13.331
I'll make myself useful
and go with Ram to fetch

05:13.421 --> 05:14.831
water in the meantime.

05:16.921 --> 05:18.301
Let's get it done, Ram.

05:18.381 --> 05:19.841
You looked like you
were just about to ask

05:19.921 --> 05:21.671
me to accompany you anyway.

05:23.181 --> 05:24.591
So lewd.

05:24.681 --> 05:26.561
[footsteps]

05:26.641 --> 05:30.101
OK, what was the idea
behind that ridiculous farce?

05:30.181 --> 05:33.271
Ram, it's really true
that I lost my memory.

05:33.351 --> 05:36.311
It isn't a lie, or a grift,
or an evil plot.

05:36.401 --> 05:37.941
Mm.

05:38.021 --> 05:39.691
My memory is gone.

05:39.781 --> 05:41.991
I remember names
and relationships

05:42.071 --> 05:43.861
and not a whole lot
more than that.

05:43.951 --> 05:45.241
Knock it off.

05:45.321 --> 05:47.451
All I know is that we
all came to this tower

05:47.531 --> 05:49.741
to get back a bunch
of stuff that we lost

05:49.831 --> 05:54.121
and that we need to pass some
exams, but otherwise, nothing.

05:54.211 --> 05:55.211
My motive is--

05:55.291 --> 05:56.251
Shut up, Barusu.

05:56.331 --> 05:57.251
No more.

05:57.331 --> 05:58.291
And Rem too. I--

05:58.381 --> 05:59.751
Barusu!

05:59.841 --> 06:01.261
Ah!

06:01.341 --> 06:03.801
[clattering]

06:03.881 --> 06:05.471
What are you playing at?

06:05.551 --> 06:06.841
What is this?

06:06.931 --> 06:09.971
What's with all these
ridiculous lies?

06:10.061 --> 06:12.561
I'm not lying to you.

06:12.641 --> 06:15.191
So you're telling me
to just trust you blindly,

06:15.271 --> 06:18.111
to believe that
you would forget Rem,

06:18.191 --> 06:21.281
something so
unfathomably stupid?

06:22.861 --> 06:25.991
Memories or not,
I'm getting Rem back.

06:26.071 --> 06:27.371
[RAM]
Ah!

06:27.451 --> 06:28.701
Who do you think you are?

06:28.781 --> 06:29.951
Get her back?

06:30.031 --> 06:31.831
You don't even
remember her, do you?

06:31.911 --> 06:35.371
Barusu, you forgot Rem!

06:35.461 --> 06:38.541
I'll still get her back,
Rem and my memories too.

06:38.631 --> 06:40.041
All of it!

06:40.131 --> 06:42.171
I'll do every damn
thing there is to do.

06:42.261 --> 06:43.671
Then we'll go home.

06:45.261 --> 06:47.141
We deserve that much at least.

06:47.221 --> 06:49.141
After everything
we've been through,

06:49.221 --> 06:52.021
this tower's done
a real number on us.

06:52.101 --> 06:52.971
Barusu!

06:53.061 --> 06:56.271
[emotional music]

06:56.351 --> 07:00.361
Ram, I'm going to get Rem
and all of my memories back.

07:00.441 --> 07:02.821
I'm going to need you
to help me do that.

07:04.321 --> 07:06.321
I'm going to need
help from all of you.

07:06.401 --> 07:08.571
You might never forgive me
for forgetting about Rem,

07:08.661 --> 07:09.911
and I understand.

07:09.991 --> 07:12.371
But still, I swear.

07:12.451 --> 07:13.911
Swear what?

07:14.001 --> 07:15.751
That I will see this through.

07:15.831 --> 07:17.671
If I ever go back on my word,

07:17.751 --> 07:20.081
then you can do
whatever you want to me.

07:20.171 --> 07:21.921
After all, I was
already careless enough

07:22.001 --> 07:23.631
to lose all of my memories.

07:23.711 --> 07:25.551
And on top of that,
I made you cry.

07:25.631 --> 07:26.881
It'd be my penance.

07:26.971 --> 07:28.301
♪ ♪

07:28.391 --> 07:29.681
Hmm.

07:29.761 --> 07:31.221
Hmm.

07:31.301 --> 07:32.431
Huh?

07:32.511 --> 07:34.021
[slapping]

07:34.971 --> 07:36.231
[thud]

07:37.601 --> 07:38.601
Who's crying?

07:38.691 --> 07:40.481
Don't be dumb.

07:40.561 --> 07:42.111
Oh, come on!

07:42.191 --> 07:44.731
It took a lot of courage
for me to say all that stuff.

07:44.821 --> 07:46.321
You got yourself
all worked up.

07:46.401 --> 07:48.111
How did that take courage?

07:48.201 --> 07:49.531
Also, a promise from you?

07:49.611 --> 07:51.161
Don't make me laugh.

07:51.241 --> 07:53.831
Wait, how many promises did
I break up until yesterday?

07:53.911 --> 07:55.951
You should be asking
how many you've kept.

07:56.041 --> 07:57.291
That's easier to count?

07:57.371 --> 07:58.711
Oh!

07:58.791 --> 08:00.081
Oh, man.

08:00.171 --> 08:02.791
This Subaru Natsuki
really is worthless, huh?

08:02.881 --> 08:05.551
Why'd you even bring
me to this tower?

08:05.631 --> 08:06.841
[RAM]
You butted in.

08:06.921 --> 08:08.421
Also, you did have
a knack for running

08:08.511 --> 08:10.341
your mouth in every situation.

08:10.431 --> 08:13.101
We could count on you
to handle odd jobs too.

08:13.181 --> 08:14.511
Is there anything else?

08:14.601 --> 08:16.471
I mean, I have short
legs, my memory's bad.

08:16.561 --> 08:19.521
And I'm also a picky eater who
doesn't know when to give up.

08:19.601 --> 08:21.651
You had short legs,
your memory was bad,

08:21.731 --> 08:24.321
and you were a picky eater who
didn't know when to give up.

08:24.401 --> 08:25.941
I walked into that.

08:26.021 --> 08:28.741
[RAM]
And

08:28.821 --> 08:30.401
you cared
a lot about Rem.

08:30.491 --> 08:31.991
[gasps]

08:33.411 --> 08:37.081
Barusu, you've truly
forgotten Rem, haven't you?

08:37.541 --> 08:39.001
Yeah.

08:39.081 --> 08:42.001
Barusu, you're truly going
to remember her, aren't you?

08:42.081 --> 08:43.791
Yeah, I will.

08:43.881 --> 08:44.961
Not just Rem.

08:45.041 --> 08:46.171
Everything else too.

08:46.251 --> 08:49.341
[sentimental music]

08:49.421 --> 08:50.341
Very well.

08:50.421 --> 08:52.301
I'll allow it, I suppose.

08:52.391 --> 08:53.601
On your feet, Barusu.

08:53.681 --> 09:00.771
♪ ♪

09:02.851 --> 09:04.111
[SUBARU]
I was--

09:04.191 --> 09:07.651
Subaru Natsuki was
definitely here, wasn't he?

09:08.651 --> 09:10.241
[RAM]
Silly.

09:10.321 --> 09:14.071
At the moment, it's just that
he's temporarily invisible.

09:14.161 --> 09:16.871
Like a flower buried under
a freezing blanket of snow,

09:16.951 --> 09:20.161
he'll emerge once more when the
cruelty of winter has passed.

09:22.331 --> 09:23.541
I'm not worried.

09:23.631 --> 09:25.631
I'm sure that's
all there is to it.

09:25.711 --> 09:26.671
Ha!

09:26.751 --> 09:33.131
♪ ♪

09:36.051 --> 09:38.891
[sighs deeply]

09:42.231 --> 09:46.111
Last time,
and the time before that,

09:46.191 --> 09:48.901
this place turned
into a complete disaster.

09:50.281 --> 09:53.531
That mess will all
happen again, and soon.

09:53.611 --> 09:56.701
I have to find a way
to stop it, no matter what,

10:00.541 --> 10:03.461
which is why, for starters--

10:05.211 --> 10:06.631
Ah!

10:06.711 --> 10:11.421
Ah! Wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait, wait, wait, wait!

10:11.511 --> 10:13.301
[sighs]

10:17.601 --> 10:19.011
Whoa, there.

10:19.101 --> 10:22.021
Don't you go taking
that fall in my place.

10:22.101 --> 10:24.691
Now, why don't you
and I have a chat?

10:24.771 --> 10:26.521
I mean, that would be murder.

10:26.601 --> 10:28.651
You need to take
responsibility.

10:31.281 --> 10:33.531
Responsibility
for murdering you?

10:33.611 --> 10:34.991
Once again,
you're saying some really

10:35.071 --> 10:36.491
weird things to me, Subaru.

10:36.571 --> 10:38.161
I'm a professional.

10:38.241 --> 10:40.581
So if I really wanted to kill
you, I'd do it differently.

10:40.661 --> 10:42.581
It would have been a whole
lot easier to do it outside,

10:42.661 --> 10:44.081
you know?

10:44.161 --> 10:46.921
Yeah, I'm sure you had
plenty of opportunities,

10:47.001 --> 10:49.041
but you didn't feel the need
to take them, right?

10:49.131 --> 10:50.791
[MEILI]
You get it, which is why--

10:50.881 --> 10:52.671
That said, you not
killing me sooner

10:52.761 --> 10:55.131
wouldn't mean a thing if you
simply didn't have a reason

10:55.221 --> 10:57.641
to do it until this morning.

10:57.721 --> 11:00.471
Or should I say until sometime
after the whole chain reaction

11:00.551 --> 11:01.851
that started last night?

11:01.931 --> 11:02.851
[sighs]

11:02.931 --> 11:04.521
Don't tell me.

11:04.601 --> 11:06.731
Were you lying about the whole
losing-your-memories thing?

11:06.811 --> 11:07.851
Oh, I see.

11:07.941 --> 11:09.401
Was this whole thing a setup?

11:09.481 --> 11:11.481
Don't get
the wrong idea, Meili.

11:11.571 --> 11:14.151
No, I wasn't lying
about losing my memory.

11:14.241 --> 11:15.991
That's why this is so serious.

11:16.071 --> 11:17.571
I'm afraid you're losing me.

11:17.651 --> 11:19.161
And now I have even
more questions.

11:19.241 --> 11:20.781
But for starters,

11:20.871 --> 11:23.581
how exactly are you planning
to finish me off here, huh?

11:23.661 --> 11:25.291
Are you gonna push
me off these stairs

11:25.371 --> 11:26.831
so you can get your revenge?

11:26.911 --> 11:28.331
My mean little
beasties aren't here

11:28.421 --> 11:29.671
to protect me
at the moment, so--

11:29.751 --> 11:31.041
I have no intention
of killing you

11:31.131 --> 11:33.711
or of hurting you,
for that matter.

11:33.801 --> 11:36.551
I plan to treat you the same
way that I have been all along.

11:36.631 --> 11:37.841
Huh?

11:37.931 --> 11:38.971
[SUBARU]
Don't worry.

11:39.051 --> 11:40.261
Thankfully,
I stopped your crime

11:40.351 --> 11:41.851
before you could carry it out.

11:41.931 --> 11:43.931
So as long as I don't go
blab about it to anyone,

11:44.021 --> 11:45.981
we can pretend it
never happened.

11:46.061 --> 11:47.351
Well, why would--

11:47.431 --> 11:48.601
All right.

11:48.691 --> 11:50.771
Now, do you understand
the situation?

11:50.861 --> 11:52.771
Trying to do anything
to me going forward

11:52.861 --> 11:54.071
is gonna be risky.

11:54.151 --> 11:55.491
And if you still want to try,

11:55.571 --> 11:58.701
then, well, let's at least
talk it over first.

11:58.781 --> 12:00.071
If something's bothering you,

12:00.161 --> 12:02.121
I'll lend an ear
and listen as best I can.

12:02.201 --> 12:03.741
[sad music]

12:03.831 --> 12:05.621
Bothering me?

12:05.701 --> 12:07.251
Bothering me?

12:07.331 --> 12:10.121
If anything bothers me,
it's this situation right now.

12:10.211 --> 12:11.711
I can't believe you.

12:11.791 --> 12:13.881
You claim that you know
what I was trying to do.

12:13.961 --> 12:14.881
What's with that?

12:14.961 --> 12:16.421
You couldn't possibly!

12:16.511 --> 12:17.921
This doesn't make any sense!

12:18.011 --> 12:21.681
It's weird, because if you
did know, then--

12:21.761 --> 12:27.021
It was only a spontaneous
act, just an impulsive choice.

12:27.101 --> 12:29.521
That's the only way you know
how to deal with your problems.

12:29.601 --> 12:31.941
You simply don't
know what else to do.

12:32.021 --> 12:35.271
And that's through
no fault of your own

12:35.361 --> 12:38.031
because murder is a habit.

12:38.111 --> 12:39.281
Ah!

12:39.361 --> 12:42.411
Stop blabbering like
you know anything!

12:42.491 --> 12:47.831
The hell could you even
possibly know about me?

12:47.911 --> 12:48.871
[SUBARU]
I know a lot!

12:48.951 --> 12:49.961
[gasps]

12:50.041 --> 12:51.081
I mean it.

12:51.161 --> 12:53.541
I know a lot about you, Meili.

12:53.631 --> 12:56.041
And this might sound kind
of creepy, but to be honest,

12:56.131 --> 12:58.171
I doubt there's anyone
else in this entire world

12:58.261 --> 13:01.261
who understands who you are
at your core better than I do.

13:03.141 --> 13:04.641
Elsa Granhiert.

13:04.721 --> 13:06.011
[gasps]

13:06.101 --> 13:08.181
[SUBARU] I'd bet
that she's the reason

13:08.271 --> 13:09.811
you tried to kill me, right?

13:09.891 --> 13:11.891
[crying]

13:13.731 --> 13:16.021
I won't let anyone--

13:16.441 --> 13:17.611
Ah!

13:20.941 --> 13:22.741
--talk as if
they understand me.

13:23.161 --> 13:25.031
[gasps]

13:25.121 --> 13:26.871
[eerie whoosh]

13:28.541 --> 13:32.751
[MEILI] I think Elsa Granhiert
was an unbelievable woman.

13:33.581 --> 13:34.291
[snarls]

13:34.751 --> 13:35.881
[thud]

13:37.541 --> 13:39.921
I've been told to bring
you back with me.

13:40.011 --> 13:42.671
That means you'll be
coming home with me today.

13:42.761 --> 13:44.551
[splash]

13:44.641 --> 13:48.561
[eerie music]

13:48.641 --> 13:49.641
Ah!

13:49.721 --> 13:51.101
[growling]

13:51.181 --> 13:52.891
[bites]

13:52.981 --> 13:54.101
Mm.

13:55.561 --> 13:56.901
What's wrong?

13:56.981 --> 13:58.191
I'm rather ticklish.

13:58.271 --> 13:59.401
Stop that.

13:59.481 --> 14:02.361
[MEILI growls]

14:03.651 --> 14:05.281
I'm not all that
particular about the clothing

14:05.371 --> 14:06.701
I wear either.

14:06.781 --> 14:10.161
But you sure do have
interesting proclivities--

14:10.241 --> 14:12.081
[growling]

14:12.161 --> 14:14.411
--and a temper to boot.

14:14.501 --> 14:15.831
That so, Meili?

14:15.921 --> 14:18.421
That is what your name is,
I assume.

14:18.501 --> 14:21.051
It's stitched into those
rags you were wearing.

14:21.131 --> 14:22.721
They could be someone else's.

14:22.801 --> 14:25.301
But not having a name
to call you is inconvenient.

14:25.391 --> 14:28.471
So you are Meili.

14:28.551 --> 14:31.561
That's what I'm going
to call you moving forward.

14:31.641 --> 14:33.521
[MEILI]
If you say you lost everything,

14:33.601 --> 14:35.601
forget any of it ever existed,

14:35.691 --> 14:37.441
it would be so easy.

14:37.521 --> 14:40.571
And then I could teach you
everything you need to know.

14:40.651 --> 14:44.401
After all, it's a mother's
job to shape her children

14:44.491 --> 14:46.531
into something better.

14:46.611 --> 14:48.161
[splat]

14:48.241 --> 14:49.911
[whimpering]

14:49.991 --> 14:54.541
I think Elsa Granhiert
was a detestable woman.

14:55.751 --> 14:57.001
[ELSA]
Are you shivering?

14:58.421 --> 14:59.631
Perhaps you're cold.

14:59.711 --> 15:01.171
Ah!
Ah!

15:01.251 --> 15:02.171
Oh!

15:02.261 --> 15:03.591
[bite sound]

15:05.841 --> 15:07.551
I told you to stop doing that.

15:07.641 --> 15:09.221
It tickles.

15:09.301 --> 15:11.351
[MEILI]
I saw every job through.

15:11.431 --> 15:14.561
I modeled my methods
after Elsa's.

15:14.641 --> 15:16.521
I learned to speak properly.

15:16.601 --> 15:20.061
I modeled my speaking
patterns after Elsa's.

15:20.151 --> 15:22.441
I even wore clothes
without fussing.

15:22.521 --> 15:26.531
I modeled my fashion
sense after Elsa's.

15:26.611 --> 15:30.491
And I made sure to keep all
of that secret from her.

15:30.571 --> 15:32.241
[wind blowing]

15:32.331 --> 15:36.501
I think Elsa Granhiert
was a dreadful woman.

15:36.581 --> 15:38.751
[ELSA] Meili,
could you braid my hair?

15:38.831 --> 15:40.461
I can't be bothered.

15:41.961 --> 15:44.261
Meili, are you listening to me?

15:44.341 --> 15:46.511
I'm asking you to braid
my hair for me.

15:46.591 --> 15:47.631
Yes, I know.

15:47.721 --> 15:48.761
I heard you.

15:48.841 --> 15:50.511
Honestly, you're such a slob.

15:50.601 --> 15:53.511
[eerie music]

15:53.601 --> 16:00.481
♪ ♪

16:00.561 --> 16:01.441
Ahm!

16:01.521 --> 16:02.441
Huh?

16:02.521 --> 16:03.441
What are you doing?

16:03.521 --> 16:04.651
That tickles.

16:04.731 --> 16:05.991
Ahm!

16:06.071 --> 16:08.111
[ELSA laughs]
You're such a funny girl.

16:08.201 --> 16:11.571
♪ ♪

16:11.661 --> 16:13.701
[MEILI] She was a huge
presence in my mind,

16:13.781 --> 16:15.871
and I didn't want
her to disappear.

16:15.951 --> 16:18.831
She was an unbelievable,
detestable, dreadful part

16:18.911 --> 16:20.461
of my life.

16:20.541 --> 16:23.881
No, calling it a "part"
wouldn't be right.

16:23.961 --> 16:25.761
It wouldn't do her justice.

16:25.841 --> 16:29.341
She was so much bigger
in existence than that.

16:29.421 --> 16:32.471
So if that all had
to be torn apart,

16:32.551 --> 16:34.851
if it had to be trampled on,

16:34.931 --> 16:38.431
if Elsa Granhiert had
to be killed by someone,

16:39.311 --> 16:41.901
then Meili Portroute--

16:44.151 --> 16:46.021
♪ ♪

16:46.111 --> 16:48.741
It would have been so much
better for all of us

16:48.821 --> 16:51.031
if you had just let me end it.

16:51.111 --> 16:53.031
[SUBARU]
Yeah, sorry.

16:53.121 --> 16:54.531
Most people take
their shoes off

16:54.621 --> 16:56.371
when entering someone's home.

16:56.451 --> 16:59.251
The Natsuki family just barges
right into the hearts of others

16:59.331 --> 17:00.911
without permission.

17:01.001 --> 17:03.381
[stretching sound]

17:03.461 --> 17:06.801
So was it for revenge?

17:06.881 --> 17:08.381
I'm not really sure.

17:08.461 --> 17:10.881
Well, let's say for a minute
that was the case.

17:10.971 --> 17:12.131
Elsa--

17:12.221 --> 17:14.641
Wouldn't have
wanted me to do that.

17:14.721 --> 17:16.601
I at least know that much.

17:19.101 --> 17:22.771
Why do you keep trying
so hard to help me?

17:22.851 --> 17:24.441
Well, if I didn't have you,

17:24.521 --> 17:25.981
then I'd have
an even bigger hole

17:26.071 --> 17:29.031
in my already-pathetic
memory, you know?

17:29.111 --> 17:31.241
Guess that's why.

17:31.321 --> 17:33.661
Meili, I get that your own
feelings are overwhelming

17:33.741 --> 17:35.571
and you don't know
what to do with them.

17:35.661 --> 17:37.451
Figuring that out
won't be easy.

17:37.541 --> 17:40.371
I doubt you'll find the answers
you're looking for right away.

17:40.451 --> 17:43.001
So let me ease
the burden for you.

17:43.081 --> 17:45.041
I won't let things go bad.

17:45.131 --> 17:47.131
Or at least I'll do
everything in my power

17:47.211 --> 17:49.001
to make sure they don't.

17:49.091 --> 17:52.721
Of course, only as long
as that's what you want too.

17:52.801 --> 17:55.221
[MEILI]
I can't believe that.

17:55.301 --> 17:56.931
It's easy for you
to say whatever

17:57.011 --> 17:58.851
you want without
a second thought.

17:58.931 --> 18:01.311
[SUBARU] Then don't consider
it a promise with me.

18:01.391 --> 18:03.641
Consider it a big
promise with all of us.

18:03.731 --> 18:04.901
Huh?

18:04.981 --> 18:07.231
[EMILIA] Yes, it's all right.
- Oh!

18:07.321 --> 18:09.401
[EMILIA] I was listening
properly to that promise.

18:09.481 --> 18:11.441
So that makes me a witness.

18:11.531 --> 18:12.651
Hmm!

18:14.071 --> 18:16.371
[SUBARU] You're seriously
a lifesaver, Emilia.

18:16.451 --> 18:18.781
Frankly, I was pretty
sure I was a goner.

18:18.871 --> 18:20.621
[EMILIA] Honestly, that's
what I should be saying.

18:20.701 --> 18:22.581
I can't believe you
tried to jump with her.

18:22.661 --> 18:25.751
I thought my heart was going
to leap right out of my chest.

18:25.831 --> 18:28.881
[MEILI] Emilia,
you heard that, everything?

18:28.961 --> 18:30.631
[EMILIA]
Yes.

18:30.711 --> 18:33.551
Subaru asked me to help you out
if you ever got into trouble.

18:33.631 --> 18:35.011
So that's what I'll do.

18:35.091 --> 18:36.141
Oh!

18:37.471 --> 18:40.761
Listen, Meili,
all those things Subaru said,

18:40.851 --> 18:45.191
I believe them, so I want
you to believe him too.

18:45.271 --> 18:47.361
Believe both of us.

18:47.441 --> 18:50.271
We're in a tower in the middle
of an ocean of sand.

18:50.361 --> 18:53.571
This place is too small for you
to make big decisions alone.

18:53.651 --> 18:56.151
Once we get out of here,
you can look for your answers

18:56.241 --> 18:57.531
in a bigger place.

18:57.621 --> 19:00.531
Until then, we'll all
really try our best.

19:00.621 --> 19:03.161
[crying]

19:03.241 --> 19:05.711
Elsa's important to me.

19:05.791 --> 19:07.881
I don't want to forget her.

19:07.961 --> 19:09.791
I know, that's fine.

19:09.881 --> 19:12.841
No need to make yourself
forget someone that you loved.

19:12.921 --> 19:15.801
That being said, it might be
better if, at the very least,

19:15.881 --> 19:18.641
you didn't try to do
things the way she did.

19:18.721 --> 19:21.011
[hair rustling]

19:21.101 --> 19:22.011
Mm!

19:22.101 --> 19:23.221
[RAM]
I see.

19:23.311 --> 19:24.641
It appears you
took care of things,

19:24.721 --> 19:26.101
not a half-bad job either.

19:26.181 --> 19:27.561
My compliments.

19:27.651 --> 19:30.021
[ECHNIDA] Perhaps I'm
overstepping by saying this,

19:30.111 --> 19:32.691
but she was so anxious
for you to return that she

19:32.781 --> 19:33.941
could hardly sit still.

19:34.031 --> 19:34.941
[RAM]
You're right.

19:35.031 --> 19:36.281
You were overstepping.

19:36.361 --> 19:37.991
Learn some restraint, Echidna.

19:38.071 --> 19:39.701
So this is
the attitude you take

19:39.781 --> 19:42.791
the moment you find out I'm
controlling this body instead?

19:42.871 --> 19:44.041
Works for me.

19:44.121 --> 19:45.251
I'll just say it.

19:45.331 --> 19:47.001
I was beside myself with worry,

19:47.081 --> 19:49.291
but I held it in because Subaru
asked me to, I suppose.

19:49.381 --> 19:50.291
Mm.

19:50.381 --> 19:51.291
Mm?

19:51.381 --> 19:52.751
[laughs]

19:52.841 --> 19:54.671
But seriously, Master,
are you sure about this?

19:54.751 --> 19:55.841
Hmm?

19:55.921 --> 19:57.301
[SHAULA]
She tried to merc you.

19:57.381 --> 19:58.931
You're gonna let
her get off scot-free?

19:59.011 --> 20:01.221
Shouldn't she get some kind
of punishment for that?

20:01.971 --> 20:03.471
It's OK.

20:03.561 --> 20:05.771
Meili's already been through
her punishment, I'd say.

20:05.851 --> 20:07.931
Thing is, in the past,

20:08.021 --> 20:10.351
she was punished without
ever knowing the reason.

20:10.441 --> 20:12.231
And things turned out this
way because no one ever

20:12.311 --> 20:13.861
bothered teaching her why.

20:13.941 --> 20:15.941
So from now on, that's my job.

20:16.031 --> 20:18.491
But of course, I'll need
your help to do it right.

20:18.571 --> 20:19.531
[SHAULA]
You want my help?

20:19.611 --> 20:20.991
Yeah, I do.

20:21.071 --> 20:23.281
Everyone in this tower is
gonna be her textbook,

20:23.371 --> 20:24.661
so make sure not to do
anything that would

20:24.741 --> 20:26.621
set a bad example for her.

20:26.701 --> 20:29.791
So then I'm included in this?

20:29.871 --> 20:31.081
Master and me?

20:31.171 --> 20:32.131
Yeah!

20:32.211 --> 20:33.381
[laughs]

20:33.461 --> 20:35.501
[SUBARU]
Uh, what's with you?

20:35.591 --> 20:36.881
Don't worry about it!

20:36.961 --> 20:38.881
Yeah, I'll turn her
into a model citizen.

20:38.971 --> 20:39.881
Just you watch!

20:39.971 --> 20:41.471
Hey, Subaru!

20:41.551 --> 20:43.391
You put weird ideas
in the naked lady's head again,

20:43.471 --> 20:44.511
didn't you?

20:44.601 --> 20:46.511
So she's not
a threat anymore.

20:46.601 --> 20:48.221
Am I understanding that right?

20:48.311 --> 20:49.601
Yep, that's right.

20:49.681 --> 20:52.271
Although it's really
all up to her.

20:52.351 --> 20:55.321
She'll learn from watching our
backs who she wants to become.

20:55.401 --> 20:58.821
So make sure yours
isn't lacking a spine.

20:58.901 --> 21:00.111
I see.

21:00.201 --> 21:01.741
It's simply a matter
of appearances.

21:01.821 --> 21:02.741
All right.

21:02.821 --> 21:04.071
You can count on me.

21:04.161 --> 21:06.581
I expect good things
from you, Mr. Knight.

21:06.661 --> 21:09.701
You and I are the closest thing
she has to a father, after all.

21:09.791 --> 21:10.541
Hmm.

21:11.791 --> 21:14.341
In that case, we'll have
to give it our best.

21:14.421 --> 21:15.341
Hmm.

21:15.421 --> 21:17.001
[laughter]

21:17.091 --> 21:19.261
You know, if I'm going
to be a real big sister

21:19.341 --> 21:20.721
to Meili, then--

21:26.891 --> 21:30.061
[SUBARU] Just a suggestion, but
why not put my amnesia aside

21:30.141 --> 21:31.061
for the time being?

21:31.141 --> 21:32.101
Huh?

21:32.191 --> 21:33.811
Don't get me wrong.

21:33.901 --> 21:36.361
I'm really happy that you want
to help me get my memory back.

21:36.441 --> 21:39.071
Except there's no way anyone
believes this is somehow

21:39.151 --> 21:40.821
unrelated to the tower.

21:40.901 --> 21:42.571
And I'm no exception.

21:42.651 --> 21:44.411
We should assume there's
a connection between this place

21:44.491 --> 21:46.451
and my amnesia, which means--

21:46.531 --> 21:48.951
Which means if we can meet
the requirements to conquer

21:49.041 --> 21:50.871
the tower and all its floors,

21:50.951 --> 21:52.581
we'll likely find the reason
for your amnesia

21:52.661 --> 21:55.881
in the process and maybe
even the key to fixing it.

21:55.961 --> 21:57.131
Is that it?

21:57.211 --> 21:58.171
That's right.

21:58.251 --> 21:59.341
Exactly.

22:00.761 --> 22:03.261
Of course, please don't
take that as me being

22:03.341 --> 22:05.391
OK with staying this way.

22:05.471 --> 22:07.971
I just want to do
what we came here for.

22:08.061 --> 22:09.561
Mm.

22:09.641 --> 22:12.311
I'll be patient, even
though that's hard.

22:12.391 --> 22:13.391
Although--

22:13.481 --> 22:15.191
Huh? What's wrong.

22:16.651 --> 22:19.321
Forgive me, but I can't
help but worry about you more

22:19.401 --> 22:20.781
than anyone else sometimes.

22:20.861 --> 22:21.901
OK?

22:21.991 --> 22:23.441
Uh, sorry.

22:23.531 --> 22:24.991
[sighs]

22:25.071 --> 22:27.531
Emilia just said what
I was going to say, I suppose.

22:27.621 --> 22:29.411
You'd better take
time to reflect.

22:29.491 --> 22:31.041
[SUBARU]
Yeah, you're right.

22:31.121 --> 22:33.751
Well, then, what's
our plan of attack?

22:33.831 --> 22:35.541
So first off,
we need to find a way

22:35.621 --> 22:37.381
to get past the next exam.

22:37.461 --> 22:39.381
And to do that,
we need to figure out

22:39.461 --> 22:41.671
what Reid's weakness is
so we can exploit it

22:41.751 --> 22:43.841
and make it to the next level.

22:43.921 --> 22:47.801
So then, I think the best place
to look would be Reid's book.

22:47.891 --> 22:49.721
Why don't we all
search the archive?

22:49.811 --> 22:52.561
[energetic music and singing]

22:52.641 --> 22:56.811
♪ ♪
